WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.550
All of that is telling me
that I'm getting better.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:06.690
And this is encouraging when you're
at that stage where you often feel

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.800
that you're not getting better.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:12.870
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann here today
and today I wanna tell you don't set

00:00:12.875 --> 00:00:14.910
long term language learning goals.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.050
That's the subject.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:20.250
If you enjoy my videos, please
subscribe, click on a bell on

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.870
the bell for notifications.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:25.470
And if you follow me on a podcast
service, please leave a comment.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:26.370
I do appreciate it.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.070
So very often, you know, people have,
I think, a vague goal of what they

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.110
wanna achieve in learning a language.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.000
They wanna be able to speak comfortably.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.220
They wanna be able to
travel and talk to people.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.990
They want to understand movies.

00:00:39.995 --> 00:00:40.980
They wanna read a book.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:41.400
They want...

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:42.960
could be any number of things.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.790
Maybe they need it for
professional reasons.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.890
So at some level we do have this
long term vision of where we want

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:55.020
to get to in a language that we're
learning and, uh, people know that.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.100
So if you buy an Assimil book or
a,  you know, a Living Language,

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.670
they'll say, you know, when you
finish this book, you'll be at B2 on

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:05.070
the European, you know, framework.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:09.720
The trouble is and, and, and I have
done this before and I'm, I'm making

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:15.420
this video because I've started into
another 90-Day Challenge in Persian so

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.720
I was thinking of what are my goals,
what do I wanna achieve in 90 days?

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:24.390
And I realized that in the past,
I've set sort of a goal for myself

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.330
of what I wanna achieve in 90 days.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:32.070
And I'll say, I wanna be able to
understand Arabic podcasts, or I

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.600
wanna be able to understand movies.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.570
And, and typically it's
a fairly ambitious goal.

00:01:36.575 --> 00:01:40.740
I want to achieve this level in
the language at the end of 90 days.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.100
The problem is that I never achieved that.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:49.979
In fact very often I have
no real measurement of how

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:51.960
far I come in those 90 days.

00:01:52.949 --> 00:01:56.850
I just realize that I'm better
than I was 90 days earlier.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:01.110
So these longer term, you know, I
want to get to this level type of

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.509
goal, very difficult to measure.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.920
And there's one thing I've learned in
language learning uh, and I think which

00:02:07.925 --> 00:02:13.484
should be applied in schools is it's
very difficult to sort of compare people,

00:02:13.484 --> 00:02:15.775
grade people based on their achievements.

00:02:16.755 --> 00:02:20.015
The only thing you can really
measure is their level of activity.

00:02:20.775 --> 00:02:24.105
That's what I would do if I ran a
classroom, I would say, how much

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.905
are you people reading my students?

00:02:25.905 --> 00:02:26.775
How much are you reading?

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:27.705
How much are you listening?

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:30.165
How much you are you
engaging with the language?

00:02:30.405 --> 00:02:33.915
If you are active, some will
do better some will do worse.

00:02:33.915 --> 00:02:38.565
Some will do better in some aspects, some
will be, will do better in other aspects.

00:02:38.895 --> 00:02:43.120
So if that's what I would demand
of people, you know, who, if I

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.670
were teaching someone, I feel I
should do the same with myself.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:50.590
So in this 90-Day Challenge, I'm
not gonna say, I want to be able

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:55.290
to understand Persian movies
or, uh, read Persian poetry.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:01.870
All I'm saying is that I am going
to set myself very short term goals

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:04.560
of what I want to achieve every day.

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:09.864
So every day I I've set in our,
when you sign up at LingQ, now this

00:03:09.885 --> 00:03:12.644
doesn't just apply to LingQ, it
could be in whatever program you're

00:03:12.644 --> 00:03:15.195
in, give yourself short term goals.

00:03:15.345 --> 00:03:19.245
In the case of LingQ, we're asked to
set, you know, whether we want to go at

00:03:19.245 --> 00:03:26.655
a leisurely pace or an insane pace, an
insane pace at link is 400 coins a day,

00:03:26.954 --> 00:03:31.125
which is actually not very demanding
as I will show you on my graphs.

00:03:31.214 --> 00:03:32.204
So I said, okay.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.140
400 coins a day.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:37.530
Bear in mind that we have now
sort of brought all of our

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:39.270
various activities together.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:45.030
And so you can earn coins by listening,
by reading, by saving LingQs, by

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:49.800
speaking, any number of activities will
contribute towards that coins total.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:53.940
And that's why I'm, that's what makes it
very easy to achieve that 400 coin level.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:58.995
If I listen for half an hour while doing
the dishes, I'll pile up a bunch of coins.

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:03.945
If I read through a lesson and save
some new words, uh, or move some

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:09.195
words to known very quickly, I, I
accumulate these 400 plus coins.

00:04:09.525 --> 00:04:15.105
So I said, okay, that's a relatively
easy goal to maintain, keeps me going,

00:04:15.465 --> 00:04:16.965
but I want a more specific goal.

00:04:16.965 --> 00:04:23.415
So I want to add 50 new word known
words to my known words, total,

00:04:23.595 --> 00:04:30.855
because here again, if I do that for
90 days, that's 4,500 more known words.

00:04:31.035 --> 00:04:34.635
So I'm now a little over
10,000 known words in Persian.

00:04:34.815 --> 00:04:36.885
That'll take me closer to 15,000.

00:04:38.294 --> 00:04:39.825
How much is that gonna help me?

00:04:39.825 --> 00:04:43.815
A lot of those words will be
lower frequency words that

00:04:43.815 --> 00:04:45.255
don't show up that often.

00:04:45.614 --> 00:04:47.625
Am I gonna understand Persian movies?

00:04:47.685 --> 00:04:53.924
I don't know, but I'm gonna focus
on those very sort of concrete goals

00:04:54.224 --> 00:05:00.645
because in chasing more known words
in chasing more coins, I'm forcing

00:05:00.645 --> 00:05:03.284
myself to engage with the language.

00:05:03.465 --> 00:05:05.445
I'm forcing myself to read more.

00:05:05.655 --> 00:05:07.484
I'm forcing myself to listen more.

00:05:08.235 --> 00:05:12.975
And in doing that, I will gradually get
better in the language, how much better?

00:05:13.245 --> 00:05:14.355
I don't really know.

00:05:14.805 --> 00:05:20.955
And I wanted to make sure that, um, I
set myself a goal that was realistic.

00:05:21.165 --> 00:05:23.205
So I'll show you on my graph here.

00:05:23.325 --> 00:05:30.135
I had a look at my, at my last 30 days,
uh, both in terms of coins accumulated

00:05:30.225 --> 00:05:32.295
and in terms of new words added.

00:05:32.685 --> 00:05:36.105
So I there's some mountains there up
and down, becasue I wasn't forcing...

00:05:36.435 --> 00:05:39.555
forcing myself sort of daily
to hit a certain level.

00:05:40.185 --> 00:05:47.025
So by looking at that, I'm comfortable
that I can easily get 400 coins a day.

00:05:47.295 --> 00:05:53.415
And, and by pushing myself a little bit,
I can reach 50, a new known words a day.

00:05:53.775 --> 00:05:56.955
And that's what I've been doing for
the last couple of days that now

00:05:56.955 --> 00:05:58.245
that I'm paying attention to it.

00:05:58.665 --> 00:06:02.925
So normally just by listening and
reading and going through text,

00:06:03.285 --> 00:06:09.555
moving the odd word to known, I'll
probably hit that 30, 35 new known

00:06:09.555 --> 00:06:15.075
words per day level, but to push it up
to 50, sometimes I have to force it.

00:06:15.435 --> 00:06:20.685
And so what I then do is go to my
vocabulary list find all the status three

00:06:20.685 --> 00:06:25.665
words, you know, I can sort by status
three words, filter by status three words.

00:06:25.725 --> 00:06:31.305
And then if I am 10 words short,
I'll go through those and find

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:34.155
10 that in fact, I already know.

00:06:34.755 --> 00:06:40.215
Now a couple of caveats, so I can
measure that known word number,

00:06:41.804 --> 00:06:43.215
but what does it really mean?

00:06:43.424 --> 00:06:48.765
We don't really know, uh, some of
the words that I claim to know, I may

00:06:48.765 --> 00:06:51.015
later on forget, so they slide back.

00:06:52.174 --> 00:06:56.804
Um, people criticize the word count
at LingQ because we count every form

00:06:56.804 --> 00:06:59.234
of the word as a different word.

00:06:59.414 --> 00:07:03.284
So run, running, runs is three words.

00:07:03.705 --> 00:07:04.424
That's not fair.

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:08.505
They say you should count
word families, maybe.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:14.160
But, uh, then it raises the
question of what is a word family?

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:22.770
So if I take the word, like we talked
about activity, so act, react, action.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.100
Are those, uh, a reactor?

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.780
Are those different words?

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.700
Are they forms of the same word?

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:32.070
Um, I don't know.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:35.340
Spoil then you have a spoiler on a car.

00:07:36.225 --> 00:07:39.015
Uh, spoils the spoils of war.

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:46.185
Uh, I think even sort of deciding
which words are part of a word family

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:49.875
and which words are in fact new
words is also somewhat arbitrary.

00:07:50.265 --> 00:07:54.305
So I prefer to go with a
way we count them at LingQ.

00:07:55.275 --> 00:07:59.775
It doesn't mean anything, you know,
objectively, you can't say I know

00:07:59.775 --> 00:08:03.315
more words than you do, or I know
more words in this language than in

00:08:03.315 --> 00:08:08.265
that language because of the number
of forms of words is gonna be greater

00:08:08.265 --> 00:08:10.635
in some languages than in others.

00:08:10.905 --> 00:08:17.985
But what it does tell you is if that
known words total increases, then

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:22.905
you know more words, you have engaged
that much more with the language you

00:08:22.905 --> 00:08:24.795
have been active with the language.

00:08:24.855 --> 00:08:27.615
And so it's an indication
that you are moving forward.

00:08:27.765 --> 00:08:32.925
This is particularly important as when
we're at the level that I'm at now, which

00:08:32.925 --> 00:08:37.275
is sort of the intermediate where I often
have the impression that I'm not getting

00:08:37.275 --> 00:08:44.505
better, but if I can look at my statistics
and see, and hopefully after 90 days I'll

00:08:44.505 --> 00:08:53.460
have add if not 4,500, at least 4,000
or so new words to my known words total.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:57.840
Probably that's gonna mean that there
are fewer and fewer blue words, in

00:08:57.845 --> 00:09:00.630
other words unknown words in my lessons.

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:04.680
It's probably going to mean that
there are more and more white words

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:06.660
on my lesson page, fewer yellow.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:10.140
All of that is telling me
that I'm getting better.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:14.280
And this is encouraging when you're
at that stage where you often feel

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.600
that you're not getting better.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:19.230
Now, how much will my
spoken Farsi improve?

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:20.220
I don't know.

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:25.830
I'm going to have a conversation with
my person tutor and I'm gonna record it.

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:28.380
I'm gonna ask her to provide subtitles.

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:31.590
And that will also be sort
of like a starting point.

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:34.710
And then at the end of the
90 days, I'll do that again.

00:09:35.145 --> 00:09:39.495
And we'll see if either you or
I can notice any improvement.

00:09:40.035 --> 00:09:44.355
So once again, it's fine to
have a long term vision that

00:09:44.355 --> 00:09:45.525
we would like to be fluent.

00:09:45.525 --> 00:09:49.395
And we would like to be able to have
intelligent conversations in a language

00:09:49.395 --> 00:09:51.285
or understand movies or read poetry.

00:09:51.584 --> 00:09:55.694
It's nice to have that as a vague
goal, but in order to push yourself

00:09:55.694 --> 00:09:59.594
in that direction, you should
not focus on the long term goals.

00:09:59.745 --> 00:10:07.455
You should focus on short term, possibly
as much as possible measurable goals

00:10:07.545 --> 00:10:13.005
that you do every day that nudge you,
that push you, that keep you going so

00:10:13.005 --> 00:10:20.085
that you eventually get closer to that
a little more vague, uh, vision of

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:21.495
where you'd like to get in the language.

00:10:21.915 --> 00:10:25.905
Now I have spoken about goals before,
so I'll leave you with a couple

00:10:25.905 --> 00:10:27.975
of videos on a similar subject.

00:10:28.395 --> 00:10:29.475
Thank you for listening.

00:10:29.565 --> 00:10:30.285
Bye for now.

